      "flags": {},
      "order": 11,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "About sound",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "MUSIC DESCRIPTION HIERARCHY\n\n1. NON-DIEGETIC MUSIC\nField: non_diegetic_music / music_style\nMeaning: audience-only background music.\nDescribe: instruments, tempo, dynamics.\nExample: A gentle solo piano at a slow tempo with soft sustained strings.\n\n2. DIEGETIC MUSIC\nField: detailed_description / shot text\nMeaning: music the characters can hear, such as a radio, TV, or performer.\nExample: A vintage radio plays softly in the corner.\n\n3. OVERALL SOUNDSCAPE\nField: overall_soundscape / soundscape\nMeaning: ambient and physical sounds only, such as wind, rain, footsteps, fabric, doors.\nNo music.\n\n4. DIALOGUE AND VOICE\nField: dialogue / <d>...</d>\nMeaning: spoken lines and lyrics.\nProtected from subject-name replacement inside <d>.\n\n5. REFERENCE AUDIO\nField: <Audio N> + retention_analysis\nfully_copy: direct reuse\npartially_copy: partial reuse or mix\nreference: style, timbre, rhythm, or content only\n\nKeep each layer in its own field. Do not put score into soundscape or scene music into non-diegetic music."
      ],
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
